extends layout

block title
  | Paramoji - API

block canonical
  link(rel="canonical" href="https://paramoji.org/api.html")

block description
  meta(name="description" content="Embed paramojis with a simple image URL and parameterize facial expressions through request parameters.")

block nav
  +nav('api')

block content
  h2.twocol#how-can-i-use-paramojis-on-my-website How to use paramojis on your website
  .twocol
    | The easiest way to link the image from <code>https://paramoji.org/paramoji.svg.php</code>.
    | The request parameters define the shape and appearance of the returned SVG image.

  h2.twocol#example Example
  .code-container.twocol
    .code
      code.card
        span.first  &lt;img src=&quot;
        | https://paramoji.org/<wbr/>paramoji.svg.php?v=70&amp;size=100&quot;/&gt;

  h2.twocol#example Parameters
  .twocol
    table.params
      tr
        th.group(colspan=2) Emotional parameters
      tr
        td <code>v</code>
        td Valence, aka pleasure, is the axis from bad to good, misery to pleasure, disagreement to agrement. 0-100, default 50
      tr
        td <code>a</code>
        td Arousal is the axis from calm to aroused, inactive to active, sleepy to alarmed. 0-100, default 50
      tr
        td <code>d</code>
        td Dominance is the axis from weakness to strength, fear to anger, submission to assertion. 0-100, default 50
      tr
        td <code>g</code>
        td Disgust is the axis from neutral to disgusted, repelled, sickened. 0-100, default 0
      tr
        td <code>c</code>
        td Contempt is the axis from neutral to smug, vain, disdainful and contemptful. 0-100, default 0
      tr
        td <code>o</code>
        td Control is the axis from uncontrolled to controlled, expressed to suppressed. 0-100, default 50
      tr
        td <code>a1, a2</code>
        td An alternative way to parameterize a and o. a1 is the arousal as shown in eyes, a2 is the arousal as shown in the mouth.
      tr
        th.group(colspan=2) Overlays
      tr
        td <code>b</code>
        td Blush from absent to maximum cheek blushing. 0-100
      tr
        td <code>t</code>
        td Tears from absent to maximum tear size. 0-100
      tr
        th.group(colspan=2) Animation
      tr
        td <code>blink_rate</code>
        td Blink rate in blinks per minute; 0 disables the animated eye blink. Repeats per minute, default 0
      tr
        td <code>speak_rate</code>
        td Speak rate in mouth movements per minute; 0 disables the animated talking mouth. Repeats per minute, default 0
      tr
        th.group(colspan=2) Rendering
      tr
        td <code>invert</code>
        td Color invert from 0 to 100 tints the background and recolors the lines through the color palette. The colors are dynamically computed to match the light and dark modes.
      tr
        td <code>size</code>
        td Size of the generated image. Set this value if the surrounding html does not define a size. Default is 100%

  .twocol
    p
      | The source code is licensed as MIT and can be accessed here:
    ul
      li
        a(href='paramoji.svg.php?showSource=true') PHP code
      li
        a(href='paramoji.js') Java Script
  .twocol
    p
      | You can use the paramoji editor to find suitable parameters.
      | To really leverage the power of paramojis these parameters must of course be dynamically derived
      | or computed.
    +try-it
